# UI tokens and primitives

- Use design tokens already defined (e.g. `--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, `--accent`, `--surface`, `--muted`) and Tailwind classes wired to them (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, etc.).
- Do **not** introduce new raw hex/HSL for core layout surfaces unless extending the token system in `app/globals.css` with team alignment.
- Do **not** use raw Tailwind palette utilities for component state. Use semantic tokens: `bg-success`, `bg-warning`, `bg-destructive`, `text-accent`, etc. If a new state color is needed, add a CSS variable in `app/globals.css` and wire it through `@theme inline`, then reference it via the corresponding utility class.
- Prefer **`components/ui`** before adding new low-level primitives. Common section pattern: `Card` + `CardHeader` + `CardTitle` + `CardContent`.
- Avoid `prose` for body text unless `@tailwindcss/typography` is configured to use the same tokens; prefer explicit `text-foreground` + link utilities (`text-accent`, underline) so typography stays on-brand.

Portal **branding** (logos, portal-specific shell): `docs/project-guidance/branding.md`.
